Legend: `!` after a field name = required (from the app's base view) —
a step form that writes such a field must not submit it empty.
`^` after a field name = shown in the app's list view: the fields users
recognize a record by — prefer them for select-card titles, stats and recall texts.
A field's human label follows in quotes where it adds information (`kosten[number] "Kosten (EUR)"`) —
use the label in every user-facing text, never the identifier.
A lookup field lists its keys after the type (`[lookup/select: a|b|c]`);
these are the ONLY valid write values — quote them into the brief verbatim;
`key=Label` shows the human label where it differs (write the key, show the label).
`·` lines carry a field's description from the app model — real process
knowledge: use it for step texts and "why we ask this" hints.
`≡` = how many records the app held when this was built — CONTEXT only
(spot empty entities, size the flow). It never chooses the data path: every
pick-a-record step goes through useRecordSearch, which counts at RUNTIME and
switches to server-side search when the entity has grown since the build
(check-intents 3k rejects an EntitySelectStep fed from a useDashboardData array).
`◈` names the input FORM each field shape wants — range → calendar
(AvailabilityRangePicker via form.range), choice → pills (ChoiceGroup), record →
select step (EntitySelectStep), stock → show the quantity, warn on overshoot.
Pick the form that fits the data; a plain field only when nothing better exists.
`⚙` lists the service methods for that entity, spelled exactly.
`✚` lists the entity's Enriched* fields and its enrich() signature,
spelled exactly — quote both verbatim; an invented enriched field or
a missing map is a guaranteed type error.

Modules — YOUR import map for the dashboard overview. NEVER paste this block,
a module path, a hook signature or an app_id into a flow or page brief: the
lanes read these files themselves through their skill, and a brief that
prescribed them cost every lane a gate round (live 07.09.2026 — wrong vSQL
and a `createRecordUrl` call copied into three flows). A brief carries the
domain: steps, eligible records, fields as `name![type: keys]`, sentences.
